# The wheel scrolls a pager — less, man, git's, bat, top: a program on
# the alternate screen that does not track the mouse. There the notches
# reach it as ↑ / ↓ keys (alternate scroll, DEC 1007, on by default in
# ghostty, xterm, iTerm2, Terminal.app and VS Code); the alternate
# screen has no scrollback of its own for the wheel to move.
# (`wheel_pty_pane.test` is the primary screen, where it does.)
#
# `less` on 200 numbered lines; ten notches down bring line 60 in.
write nums.txt ""
shell seq 1 200 | sed 's/^/row-/' > nums.txt
command view.toggle_tree
ex term less nums.txt
wait 1200
expect screen contains "row-1"
scroll 20 20 down
scroll 20 20 down
scroll 20 20 down
scroll 20 20 down
scroll 20 20 down
scroll 20 20 down
scroll 20 20 down
scroll 20 20 down
scroll 20 20 down
scroll 20 20 down
wait 400
expect screen contains "row-60"
